# 🦈 Wireshark Notes – Analysis Tools

## 📊 Statistics Overview
- Provides summary of captured packets
- Helps identify traffic patterns and anomalies
- Located under: `Statistics` menu

---

## 🌐 Resolve Addresses (Name Resolution)
- Converts numeric values into readable names

### Types:
- MAC → Vendor name  
- IP → Hostname  
- Port → Service name  

### Benefits:
- Improves readability
- Easier packet analysis

### Path:
`View → Name Resolution`

---

## 🧬 Protocol Hierarchy
- Displays distribution of protocols in capture

### Shows:
- Protocol percentages  
- Packet counts  
- Traffic composition  

### Use:
- Identify dominant protocols (HTTP, TCP, DNS)
- Detect unusual traffic

---

## 💬 Conversations
- Tracks communication between two endpoints

### Types:
- Ethernet  
- IPv4 / IPv6  
- TCP / UDP  

### Shows:
- Source & Destination  
- Packet count  
- Bytes transferred  

### Use:
- Identify heavy traffic pairs
- Analyze connections

---

## 🔗 Endpoints
- Lists all unique devices in the capture

### Shows:
- IP / MAC address  
- Packets sent/received  
- Bytes sent/received  

### Use:
- Identify active devices
- Detect suspicious hosts

---

## 📛 Name Resolution (Detailed)
- Converts addresses into readable formats

### Types:
- MAC Resolution → Manufacturer  
- Network Resolution → DNS  
- Transport Resolution → Port to service  

### Note:
- Can slow down analysis if enabled

---

## 📈 I/O Graphs
- Visual representation of traffic over time

### Features:
- Packets/bytes per second  
- Filter-based graphs  
- Multiple graphs support  

### Use:
- Detect spikes in traffic  
- Analyze bandwidth  
- Identify anomalies  

---

